LLVM 23 defaults gfx11/gfx12 to +real-true16 mode, which requires .l/.h
subregister suffixes on 16-bit instructions (e.g. v_cvt_f16_f32 v0.l, v1).
Tensile 7.14 emits the legacy fake16 syntax (no suffix), so the integrated
assembler rejects it with "operands are not valid for this GPU or mode".

Disable real-true16 for the integrated assembler via -Xclangas -target-feature.
The ROCm LLVM fork defaults to fake16, so this only bites when building
against system LLVM 23.
--- a/Tensile/KernelWriterAssembly.py
+++ b/Tensile/KernelWriterAssembly.py
@@ -281,6 +281,13 @@
 
     rv += ['-mcpu=' + gfxName(isa)]
 
+    # LLVM 23 defaults gfx11/gfx12 to +real-true16 mode, which requires
+    # .l/.h subregister suffixes on 16-bit instructions. Tensile emits the
+    # legacy fake16 syntax (no suffix), so disable real-true16 for the
+    # integrated assembler.
+    if isa[0] >= 11:
+      rv += ['-Xclangas', '-target-feature', '-Xclangas', '-real-true16']
+
     if wavefrontSize == 64:
       rv += ['-mwavefrontsize64']
     else:
